          "comment": "Five-time winner; not at his best the last twice and a visor replaces cheekpieces",
          "spotlight": "2m3f success at Carlisle in April (good), his fifth career win; not at his best the last twice and a visor replaces cheekpieces.",
          "medical": [
            {
              "date": "2023-08-16",
              "type": "Wind Surgery"
            }
          ],
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2023-05-13",
              "horse": "Willaston",
              "horse_id": "3560290",
              "race": "Pertemps Network Long Distance Handicap Hurdle (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "838425",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "24.5",
              "distance_y": "5338",
              "quote": "We were surprised at Cheltenham. We thought Willaston might get a place there if we were lucky, but he finished like a train and I think this is what he wants - three miles on good ground. Jamie (Hamilton) thinks he may be a Pertemps horse. In the long-term he's a chaser. I know he fell on his chasing debut, but we can put that behind us. But what's the point at the moment when he can win hurdles like that? - Tim Walford, trainer's father."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-04-19",
              "horse": "Willaston",
              "horse_id": "3560290",
              "race": "Kingston Stud Handicap Hurdle (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "835892",
              "course": "Cheltenham",
              "course_id": "crs_286",
              "distance_f": "20.5",
              "distance_y": "4456",
              "quote": "We knew Willaston was in good form coming into it and his first run of the season was great. I thought we might nick a place but I'd be lying if I thought we'd win. He's a lovely horse, his owner bought him for £11,000 and he's been great. He will be a chaser but whether we'll go jumping fences in the new season I'm not sure. This has topped off a wonderful season for the team - Mark Walford, trainer."
            }
          ],
